    {
      "d2_id": "lower.strategies.dense.dense_body",
      "dot_id": "node_n055",
      "parent_d2_id": "lower.strategies.dense",
      "parent_dot_id": "cluster_n054",
      "kind": "node",
      "label": "Pack the ragged flat list into a rectangle, so every  \nshape is fixed at compile time.  \nNeeded because an offset computed from data does not  \nlower under compilation (torch-spyre#3508) — exactly  \nthe arithmetic that flash relies on.  \nEager tolerates it; compiled mode, our target, does not.\n\n· build an additive mask [S, 1, L, L] marking padding  \nand cross-request slots  \n· build three index lists, then gather Q / K / V into  \n[S, H, L, D]  \n· one fused SDPA kernel per (S, L), then gather the  \nresults back out\n\n**Shape axes: T for the body, (S, L) for attention.  \nTwo sets of buckets to warm.**\n\nCosts: the mask grows with L², plus index lists and a  \nbarrier per gather.  \nWorks today. This is the current implementation.",
      "source_shape": "text",
      "dot_shape": "plaintext",
      "differences": [
        "width placement/sizing omitted",
        "markdown uses the same plain multiline text as Mermaid"
      ]
    },
