    {
      "d2_id": "lower.strategies.flash.flash_body",
      "dot_id": "node_n057",
      "parent_d2_id": "lower.strategies.flash",
      "parent_dot_id": "cluster_n056",
      "kind": "node",
      "label": "Never materialise the rectangle.  \nEach block of queries reads its request's offset from  \nthe metadata at runtime, and works directly on the flat  \nlist, carrying a running softmax maximum and sum.  \nThat is the online-softmax structure the Spyre decoder  \nalready uses over KV pages.\n\n· no [S, 1, L, L] mask; request boundaries are the offsets  \n· no gather_pack / gather_unpack; the kernel reads the  \nflat list directly  \n· no per-layer index lists, so no per-gather barriers\n\n**Shape axis: block count, bucketed like the decoder's  \npage loop. L disappears.**\n\nBoth upstream backends already work this way, neither  \npadding into a rectangle.  \nFlash attention consumes the flat list with  \ncu_seqlens_q = query_start_loc, and the CPU backend  \npasses query[:num_actual_tokens] to a C++ kernel.",
      "source_shape": "text",
      "dot_shape": "plaintext",
