      "kind": "node",
      "label": "· the second shape axis collapses; bucket T and a block count,  \nmuch closer to upstream's single axis  \n· the batch-shape tables box disappears, and with it the  \nper-layer rebuild problem and its barriers  \n· gather_pack / SDPA / gather_unpack collapse into one  \nblocked-attention kernel  \n· the mask's L² growth at long prompts disappears, today's  \nlargest untested risk\n\nOpen question: whether a Spyre kernel can do the runtime  \noffset arithmetic this depends on. If it cannot, the block  \ncount stays bucketed.  \nEverything else holds either way: padding seam, unpadded  \nmetadata, warmup, compilation mode.",
